{#- What three fixed phrases of the work and concern views mean, said once in a prompt (2026-11-15: the situation auditor
    read each up to 18 times, once per work object or concern). A reader shown many of them states this in its system
    prompt and its input sets `explained_once` (shared/work/portfolio.j2, concern_view.j2, work_progress.j2 then leave
    it out); a concern list rendered without that states the lines it needs once at its head (concern_view.j2).
    `explain_failures`, `explain_carried`, `explain_record` switch a line off when false. Terse readers
    (`wording_explained`) read shared/work/wording_explained.j2, which includes the carried and record lines from here
    (each sentence lives in one file). -#}
{% if explain_failures | default(true) -%}
- Historical failure totals (a work object's "goal failures judged by finalizer") do not request another user decision.
  Follow current finalizer instructions and the user's recorded answers; do not re-ask a resolved question because
  of that tally.
{% endif -%}
{% if explain_carried | default(true) -%}
- A work "In progress" or "On hold" is carried by the assistant until every step is done, or abandoned with a reason.
{% endif -%}
{% if explain_record | default(true) -%}
- A concern's record is oldest first: a summary of the older notes, then every note since, each with when it was
  written.
{% endif -%}
